# poetry
poetry.lock

# Everything this repo generates by running experiments: results, optimizer
# traces, model cache, MLflow local store. Regenerated by running the suite -
# see CLAUDE.md - never hand-edited, so none of it belongs in git.
# .logs/
mlflow.db
# SQLite sidecars. mlflow.db was switched to WAL journaling so a parallel sweep's
# many concurrent writers do not serialize on a whole-file lock; WAL mode creates
# these two beside it. They are pure runtime state - never commit them.
mlflow.db-wal
mlflow.db-shm
# The execution-time study's own trees (docs/EXECUTION_TIME_STUDY_PLAN.md).
# Kept OUT of .logs/ and mlflow.db on purpose: those hold the accuracy/CR
# experiments' traces and runs, and this study must not write into them.
.logs_exectime/
mlflow_exectime.db
mlflow_exectime.db-wal
mlflow_exectime.db-shm
exectime_run.log
mlruns/
mlartifacts/
out/
.tmp/

# Raw dataset directories. These are machine-local symlinks into a Laconic
# checkout (several GB of archives, not copied into this repo). Git stores a
# symlink's target verbatim, so committing them bakes one person's absolute
# path into the repo and dangles everywhere else - each checkout creates its
# own. See "Datasets" in README.md.

# Pre-rewrite snapshots taken by scripts/fix_forecasting_test_window.py
.backups/

# Per-sweep driver logs. Each long sweep writes its console output and a state
# note under a dot-directory named after the sweep (.seed128_logs/,
# .budget150_logs/, ...) plus a *_bootstrap.log beside it. They record one
# machine's run, not the experiment - the experiment is the manifest in
# cfg/suites/ and the CSVs under results/.
.*_logs/
.*_bootstrap.log

# Same rule, one level in: scripts/run_seed_gap.py writes the sweep's console
# output (one file per shard), its pid file and a generated single-dataset cfg
# tree under .logs/seed_gap/. That is driver state for one machine's run, not
# the experiment - the experiment is the manifests in cfg/suites/, the CSVs
# under results/ and the optimizer traces elsewhere in .logs/.
.logs/seed_gap/

# Ad-hoc per-dataset probe logs written at the repo root by one-off measurements.
/hentropy_*.log
/ieeeppg_baselines.log

# Built artifacts of the batched SerfXOR binding, and the pinned Serf checkout
# build.sh clones to build it. wrapper.cpp, build.sh and README.md reproduce
# both; a .so is ABI- and machine-specific and the Serf source is CC BY-NC (see
# README.md), so neither is vendored into the repo.
compression/lib/batch_serfxor/build/
compression/lib/batch_serfxor/serf/
compression/lib/batch_pyserf*.so

# JVM fatal-error logs and core dumps, written at the repo root when a process is
# killed mid-call (MixPiece runs a JVM through jpype). Diagnostics, not content.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
core.[0-9]*
